oop forming  in many GPCRs the seven helix bundle is  not perfectly symmetrical and helix four  is bound towards the outside of the  bundle form the intracellular loop  between helix 3 and the extracellular  one between HeLa C's 4 and 5 but let the  helix 4 dangle on the side  Connect Gila sees three and five by  lining area three b25 a matching the  position of the symbol with four  diamonds  connect Ulysses five and six by lining  areas by B and 6a matching the position  of the raindrop symbols  now you will notice the last  intracellular loop forming  Connect Gila sees six and seven by  aligning areas 6b and 7a matching the  position of the flower symbols now you  will notice the last extracellular loop  forming  finish the model by taping together  helix seven and one be sure to align the  semi-transparent gray area between 7b  and 1a and match the positions of the  Sun symbol  now you will notice the cavity at the  top that represents the ligand binding  site  you
 

